Data visualisation converts raw data into charts and graphs, so that:
- patterns, trends and outliers are seen quickly;
- complex results are easier to interpret and communicate to technical and non-technical audiences;
- errors and misunderstandings are reduced.

Ethical use of data protects people and builds trust:
- it respects privacy and confidentiality, with data collected by consent and used only for its intended purpose;
- it prevents discrimination and misuse of models;
- it keeps data-driven decisions fair, accurate and trusted.
